# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore — files Git must NEVER commit.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
#   Build artifacts (dist/, node_modules/) are large, machine-generated, and
#   differ per OS. Committing them bloats the repo and causes merge conflicts.
#   Vercel / CI rebuilds them from package.json + pnpm-lock.yaml on deploy.
#   JUNIOR: if `git status` shows thousands of files after `pnpm install`,
#   this file is misconfigured — do NOT `git add -f` them, fix the rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies — JUNIOR: reinstall with `pnpm install` after cloning.
# Never commit: ~200MB, OS-specific binaries inside.
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build outputs — JUNIOR: regenerating with `pnpm build` recreates these.
# `dist` = production site, `server` = legacy SSR output, `.vercel`/`.output`
# = deploy-provider caches. AI NOTE: `server/` is ignored for history reasons
# (older Qwik adapters emitted there); harmless if the folder is absent.
dist
server
.vercel
.output

# TypeScript incremental build info — JUNIOR: local compiler cache that
# speeds up `tsc --incremental`. Safe to delete; tsc recreates it.
*.tsbuildinfo

# OS / editor noise — JUNIOR: .DS_Store (macOS Finder), Thumbs.db (Windows),
# *.log (debug output), .vscode/* (personal editor settings).
# The `!` exception keeps shared extension recommendations.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
